<p>... and as it appeared in 2007</p>

<p>The building was later retrofitted with a modern air conditioning system, including the elimination of several windows on its south face and replacement of the remaining windows. The building is among five area government projects constructed and dedicated to the men and women of the military in World War I and died in service to their country. The North Dakota Memorial Bridge (which was replaced in 2008 with a bridge designated as the Liberty Memorial Bridge), Memorial Highway (which connects the east side of Mandan's Main Street with the original west end of Bismarck's Main Street at a former Washington Street railroad track viaduct), the Liberty Memorial Building (current ND State Library on the state capitol grounds) and Bismarck's World War Memorial Building honor these servicemen and women.This building currently houses the City of Mandan Administrative offices, including the water department, which is appropriately located over the former swimming pool. The pool was filled in the late 1960s after continued problems with the water treatment system. A new larger outdoor public pool was constructed south of today's Custer Elementary Grade School in central Mandan as its replacement.</p>
